<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    CYAC.Port.Core — the native C# port's engine core (doc/native-port-plan.md, BUILDING since
    2026-08-24).  Clean, idiomatic C#: NOT a citizen of the instruction-counting emulator.

    DEPENDENCY RULE (plan §9b + transform-plan L2): this project references NO other project at
    all.  It must NEVER reference CYAC.Emulator / CYAC.Emulator.*, and as of port batch 2 T7 it no
    longer references CYAC.Formats either: the runtime reads the transformed open-format data tree,
    not the original assets.  The emulator is a dev-side reference instrument that may reference
    THIS assembly to certify it — never the other way around.

    Schema/state_schema.json = the exported scanner.py state schema (E2), the data-model ground
    truth.  Regenerate with `python3 doc/port_schema_export.py`; never hand-edit.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>preview</LangVersion>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <RootNamespace>CYAC.Port.Core</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Schema\state_schema.json" LogicalName="CYAC.Port.Core.Schema.state_schema.json" />
    <!-- ★ VECTOR MARKINGS (2026-09-11, doc/port-vector-markings-spec.md): the port's OWN pictures,
         font and per-class placements — knowledge, not shipped data — embedded so a runtime needs
         no directory to draw them.  An override directory (fly - -markings-dir) overlays them.
         Placements ship as DIFFS over the base MarkingBootstrap generates from the data tree
         (placements/<class>.diff.json → resource "…placements.<class>.diff.json"); the base's
         numbers come from the original meshes and are never embedded. -->
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Markings\font.json" LogicalName="CYAC.Port.Core.Markings.font.json" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Markings\pictures\*.json" LogicalName="CYAC.Port.Core.Markings.pictures.%(Filename).json" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Markings\placements\*.diff.json" LogicalName="CYAC.Port.Core.Markings.placements.%(Filename).json" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    NO ProjectReference. ~~The on-disk format codecs (CYAC.Formats)~~ *(retired 2026-08-25, port
    batch 2 T7 — transform-plan law L2: "the runtime reads the data tree only". This assembly loads
    JSON/PNG/WAV documents that `cyac-transform` produced and never opens a `.lib` or the
    executable, so CYAC.Formats is now a TRANSFORM-TIME dependency only. The test project still
    references it (its fixtures compare the tree against the shipping assets) and so does
    CYAC.Port.Transform.)*

    The dependency rule (native-port-plan §9b) still stands and is now stricter than it was: this
    project references NOTHING but the BCL, and never CYAC.Emulator*.
    `PortDataLoaderTests.PortCoreReferencesNeitherFormatsNorTheEmulator` asserts it by reflection.
  -->

</Project>
